<h2>Hypothesis</h2>
<p>
  This is not a claim about nature but a claim about the instrument: the engine, run in
  the shape the published BFF work used, reproduces the emergence of self-replicators.
  A well-mixed soup — every interaction pairs a cell with a partner drawn uniformly from
  the whole world — of 2<sup>17</sup> tapes should leave the random-soup regime within
  the epoch budget: <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> collapses,
  <span class="mono">replicator_count</span> rises off zero and stays there.
</p>
<p>
  The falsifier is blunt. If this control never transitions,
  suspect the interpreter or the pairing rule, not the hypothesis:
  the sweeps of DESIGN §1.3 are only worth reading once the engine has been shown to
  produce the effect they measure.
</p>

<h2>Method</h2>
<p>
  A 512×256 torus — 131 072 cells, 2<sup>17</sup> tapes — of 64-byte tapes
  (<span class="mono">tape_len = 64</span>), <span class="mono">radius = 0</span> for the
  well-mixed neighbourhood, <span class="mono">max_steps = 8192</span> per interaction,
  50 000 epochs per run. Two arms, <span class="mono">mutation_rate = 0</span> and the
  engine default <span class="mono">2<sup>-12</sup> = 2.44 × 10<sup>-4</sup></span>, with
  seeds 1, 2 and 3 each: six runs. Sampling is sparse for a world this size —
  <span class="mono">sample_every = 50</span> and
  <span class="mono">snapshot_every = 2000</span>, 25 full-world snapshots per run instead
  of the 500 the engine's default cadence would write. The runs carry queue priority 10,
  ahead of every sweep, because nothing else in the lab means anything until they land.
</p>

<h2>Result</h2>
<p>
  Partial, and not the reading the hypothesis asked for. This is a partial and not a claim
  for three reasons: one mutated seed of three has moved, the epoch horizon is nowhere near
  reached, and the census that would make the move mean something is unresolved. What
  follows states shapes; the per-run numbers behind them drift with every sample and are in
  the evidence table below, which reads the runs live.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>The instrument produces the signature.</strong> The mutated arm has transitioned
  in one of three seeds, and it transitioned the way the mutation-rate sweep's flagged runs
  do: <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> collapses inside a few sampling intervals,
  <span class="mono">distinct_tapes</span> falls from one-per-cell and keeps falling,
  <span class="mono">copy_rate</span> lifts off exactly zero,
  <span class="mono">op_density</span> rises and <span class="mono">entropy_bits</span>
  drops — one joint move, not five independent ones. The three
  <span class="mono">mutation_rate = 0</span> controls sit at the random-soup baseline and
  the remaining two mutated seeds have not moved. So the interpreter and the pairing rule
  do produce the published signature in the published shape; the harness is not what the
  sweeps were measuring.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>But the census reads zero.</strong> <span class="mono">replicator_count</span> is
  zero at every snapshot inspected, and a rescore with the ranking cut widened to the top
  16, 64 and 256 tapes returns metrics identical at all three widths, with no ranked tape
  passing the 3-of-4 replicator trial — on this control and on the mutation-rate runs that
  collapsed hardest alike. Truncation of the ranking is ruled out. A collapse in tape
  statistics is not a count of copiers, so this control is not yet evidence of
  self-replicators, and the falsifier above is neither triggered nor retired.
</p>

<h2>What the census shows</h2>
<p>
  The census is less flat than flickering: inside the plateau that follows a collapse a
  single sample read a non-zero count with zero on both sides of it, while compression,
  diversity and copy rate moved together across that whole stretch. The mutation-rate
  sweep shows the same pattern, its detector and its census disagreeing in both
  directions. Two readings are open. Either a replicating lineage is there and the 3-of-4
  trial rule misses it — a strict test, applied to a handful of ranked tapes — or the
  collapse is degenerate: tape content converging on something compressible that copies
  nothing. Nothing measured so far separates them, and the second reading would make the
  transition detector of DESIGN §1.2 a weaker observable than the sweeps have been treating
  it as.
</p>
<p>
  The next measurement is a rescore at the first snapshot taken after a collapse rather
  than at the pre-collapse snapshots rescored so far, plus a persistence requirement on the
  census: a count that survives consecutive samples, not one that appears in a single one.
</p>
<p>
  The gap in these runs is harness history, not signal. All six failed between epoch 546
  and epoch 633 against a read limit in the runner's lab-mode client — its 10 MiB cap on an
  API response, too small for a world this size — fixed by PR #17, which raised the limit
  to 256 MiB, and they were requeued from their last snapshot. A container recreate
  released them a second time, and they resumed from their snapshots again.
</p>
<p>
  Until the census resolves, no sweep on this site is readable as a clean negative result.
  The mutation-rate finding is held on that basis.
</p>
